IMPORT prelude

-- Public Interest Disclosure Act 2003 (WA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The Act counts its periods in calendar months: s 10(1) "not more than 3 months after the disclosure is
-- made", s 7A(2)(b) "the period ending 6 months after the disclosure was made". The person's own period under s 17(1)(a)
-- is the one the person investigating specifies, counted here in days.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2003`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a number of days after a day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` `the days` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `the days`)

-- Whether the first day is strictly before the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `is earlier than` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0)

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF m EQUALS 2
        THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
        IF m EQUALS 4 OR m EQUALS 6 OR m EQUALS 9 OR m EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
        OTHERWISE 31

-- The day a number of calendar months after a day: the same day of the month that many months on; where that month has
-- no such day (31 August plus 6 months), the last day of that month (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` `the months` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `the months`
        `the month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS ((`the month index` MINUS (`the month index` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the last day of that month` MEANS `the number of days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`
        `the day number` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the day` GREATER THAN `the last day of that month`
            THEN `the last day of that month`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the day`
